# rm(1)

## NAME

rm - remove files or directories

## SYNOPSIS

    rm [-rRf] file...

## DESCRIPTION

Removes files. `.`, `..` and `/` are refused.

## OPTIONS

- `-r, -R`: remove directories and their contents
- `-f`: ignore files that do not exist

## EXIT STATUS

- `0`: success
- `1`: an error occurred for some operand
- `2`: usage error

## SEE ALSO

rmdir(1)
